---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';

const updated = 'October 23, 2026';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title={`Terms of Use — ${SITE_TITLE}`}
			description="The terms for buying and using YTCPM Bot: licenses, devices, crypto payments, activation, support and acceptable use."
		/>
		<style>
			main {
				padding: 0;
			}
			.band {
				background: var(--surface);
				border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light));
				padding: 2.8em 0 2.4em;
			}
			.band h1 {
				font-size: clamp(2em, 4.6vw, 2.9em);
			}
			.band p {
				color: rgb(var(--gray-dark));
			}
			.body {
				padding: 2.6em 0 0.5em;
			}
			.inner {
				max-width: 760px;
			}
			.inner h2 {
				font-size: 1.35em;
				margin: 1.5em 0 0.5em;
			}
			.inner h2:first-child {
				margin-top: 0;
			}
			.inner p,
			.inner li {
				line-height: 1.7;
				color: rgb(var(--gray-dark));
			}
			.inner ul {
				margin: 0.4em 0 1em;
			}
		</style>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<section class="band bleed">
				<div class="wrap">
					<h1>Terms of Use</h1>
					<p>Last updated: {updated}</p>
				</div>
			</section>
			<section class="body bleed">
				<div class="wrap">
					<div class="inner">
						<h2>1. The product</h2>
						<p>
							YTCPM Bot is a standalone Windows application. Buying a plan gives you
							a license to use the software for the duration and number of devices
							of that plan, as shown on the <a href="/pricing">pricing page</a>. The
							current version and download are on the <a href="/download">download
							page</a>. Your license is for your own use — please don't redistribute
							the software or share your sign-in credentials.
						</p>

						<h2>2. Payment</h2>
						<p>
							Payment is 100% in advance, in one of the cryptocurrencies shown at
							checkout (USDT, BTC or ETH), at the USD prices listed for each plan.
							An order is confirmed when the payment is verified. Send payments only
							to the address shown on your order page — a payment sent to a wrong
							address or network cannot be recovered by us.
						</p>

						<h2>3. Activation</h2>
						<p>
							After your payment is confirmed, your license is activated and the
							admin contacts you within 24 hours. Activation requires the correct
							order details and payment proof, so submit them carefully.
						</p>

						<h2>4. Devices and resets</h2>
						<p>
							Each plan covers the number of devices stated for it. The device count
							resets every 10 days while your license is active. If you change
							hardware and need a manual reset, contact support — a manual reset can
							take up to 24 hours.
						</p>

						<h2>5. Support</h2>
						<p>
							Support is available 6 days a week, with night support from 7:00 PM to
							7:00 AM, through the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
						</p>

						<h2>6. Acceptable use</h2>
						<p>
							You are responsible for your own accounts, content and activity, and
							for complying with the law and with the terms of any third-party
							platform you use the software with. Don't use the software for
							unlawful purposes.
						</p>

						<h2>7. No affiliation, no earnings guarantee</h2>
						<p>
							YTCPM Bot is an independent tool and is not affiliated with or
							endorsed by YouTube or Google. CPM figures and results depend on many
							factors outside our control; any figures mentioned on this site are
							estimates, not guarantees of earnings or results.
						</p>

						<h2>8. Availability and changes</h2>
						<p>
							We may update the software and this website, and features may change
							over time. We work to keep the service available but don't guarantee
							uninterrupted access.
						</p>

						<h2>9. Liability</h2>
						<p>
							The software is provided "as is". To the extent allowed by law, our
							liability for any claim connected with the software or this site is
							limited to the amount you paid for your current license.
						</p>

						<h2>10. Changes to these terms</h2>
						<p>
							If these terms change, the new version will be posted on this page
							with an updated date. Questions about the terms: use the
							<a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
						</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
